course: dictionary
lesson: 12313
title: Correspond: match, equal, or write
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word correspond has three main meanings. It can mean two things match or fit together. It can mean one thing is like or equal to another in a different system. It can also mean writing letters or emails to someone over time. The context tells you which meaning is right.
explain: «Each number on the card corresponds to a picture.» Here the numbers match the pictures, so each number goes with one picture. Try the check: swap in match and read the sentence again. If it still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
explain: «Our pen pal in Japan corresponds with us every month.» There is no matching here. The clue is every month, which tells you the pen pal writes letters over time. Read the words around a word, and they will tell you what it means.
fact: Correspond means to match or fit together with something else.
fact: «Correspond to» usually means match, as in «The numbers correspond to the pictures.»
fact: «Correspond with» can mean writing letters or emails to someone over time, as in «Ella corresponds with her pen pal.»
fact: In maths, sides and angles that correspond are in matching positions in two shapes.
fact: Synonyms for correspond in the matching sense include match, fit and agree, but correspond can also mean being equal to something in a different system: «A year 6 class roughly corresponds to a fifth grade in America.»
exercise: «Each number on the card corresponds to a picture.» What does corresponds mean here? | Is bigger than | Is lost in | Runs away from | *Matches or goes with
exercise: In maths, two shapes have sides that correspond. What does that mean? | They are hidden under the shape | They are the longest sides | They are the same colour | *They are in matching positions in both shapes
exercise: «Our pen pal in Japan corresponds with me every month.» What does corresponds with mean here? | Counts my money | Visits me every month | *Writes letters to me over time | Shouts at me each month
test: «The answers must correspond to the questions.» Which word could replace correspond here? | Jump | Forget | *Match | Hide
test: «A year 6 class roughly corresponds to a fifth grade in America.» What does corresponds mean here? | Is hidden inside | *Is about the same as | Is much bigger than | Is the opposite of
exam: Which sentence uses correspond to mean writing letters to someone? | The numbers correspond to the pictures. | The answers correspond to the questions. | The two shapes correspond closely. | *Ella and her pen pal correspond every week.
